      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transport Aurangabad</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The destination delivery handover for two‑wheelers and motorcycles is a critical checkpoint that guarantees the vehicle reaches the consignee in the exact condition documented at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By conducting a daylight re‑inspection, cross‑checking the odometer, and obtaining a signed condition sign‑off, both the logistics provider and the recipient protect themselves against disputes and ensure transparency throughout the transit process.</span></li></ul>

<h3>1. Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</h3>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Visual comparison with pickup photos:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Inspectors examine the motorcycle under natural light, matching every angle of the current vehicle to the high‑resolution images taken at the origin. This includes body panels, paint finish, chrome trims, mirrors, and any accessories.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Damage identification:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Any new scratches, dents, or broken components are noted immediately. Photographic evidence of any discrepancies is captured on site to supplement the handover record.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Functional checks:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">While the primary focus is visual, basic functional items such as lights, horn, and indicator operation are verified to ensure the bike is road‑ready.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>2. Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reading capture:</strong> The odometer is read directly from the instrument cluster and recorded to the nearest kilometre or mile.</li>
<li><strong>Cross‑reference with LR bilty:</strong> The recorded figure is compared with the mileage noted on the Lorry Receipt (LR) bilty, which reflects the odometer reading at the time of loading.</li>
<li><strong>Discrepancy handling:</strong> If a variance exceeds the agreed tolerance (typically 5‑10 km), the inspector documents the difference, informs both parties, and may require a joint re‑inspection before release.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Signed Condition Sign‑off</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Recipient acknowledgment:</strong> The consignee reviews the inspection checklist, photographs, and odometer verification. Once satisfied, they sign the handover form, confirming acceptance of the vehicle’s condition.</li>
<li><strong>Provider’s declaration:</strong> The logistics representative also signs, attesting that the handover was completed in accordance with the documented procedure.</li>
<li><strong>Retention of records:</strong> Both signatures, along with the inspection photos and odometer data, are stored digitally for future reference and dispute resolution.</li>
</ul>

<p>By rigorously following these three steps—daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed condition sign‑off—the delivery process safeguards the integrity of the two‑wheeler’s condition, minimizes post‑delivery claims, and builds trust between the shipper, carrier, and recipient.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


